### Rotating Card (Hover Effect)

Below is a minimal example of a card that flips (rotates) when you hover over it.  
It uses **CSS 3D transforms** and a small amount of JavaScript only if you want to add interactivity beyond the hover effect.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* 1. Set up the perspective for the container */
.card-container {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* 2. The card itself – a 3D wrapper */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Allows children to be positioned in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth animation */
}

/* 3. Front and back faces */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide the back face when it's turned away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.card-front {
  background: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

.card-back {
  background: #f8f8f8;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Position the back face behind the front */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #555;
}

/* 4. Hover effect – flip the card */
.card-container:hover .card {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-container">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | Explanation |
|------|-------------|
| **1. Perspective** | The `.card-container` gives the 3D space. Without it, the rotation would look flat. |
| **2. Card wrapper** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` allows child elements to maintain their 3D positions. |
| **3. Faces** | Both faces are absolutely positioned on top of each other. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the back side when it’s turned away. |
| **4. Hover** | On hover, the `.card` is rotated 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back face. |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add images inside the faces. You can also change the rotation axis (`rotateX`, `rotateZ`) or the angle to create different effects.
